9. Result
The sand, gravel and charcoal filter reduces visible suspended particles and improves the apparent clarity of the water. The turbidity sensor can be used to demonstrate the change quantitatively.
10. Advantages
Low cost
Easy to construct
Uses easily available materials
Simple to demonstrate
Does not require electricity for the basic filter
11. Limitations
It does not remove all microorganisms.
It may not remove all dissolved chemicals or salts.
Clear-looking water is not necessarily safe to drink.
The filter materials must be clean.
12. Conclusion
The project demonstrates how different filtration layers can remove suspended impurities from water. By adding an Arduino and turbidity sensor, the improvement in water clarity can also be measured electronically.